A Rust implementation of the CodeRankEmbed encoder for the CPU and for
Vulkan GPUs, provided under MIT (LICENSE). It reads the model's published
files and ships none of its weights; tests/data/config.json is the model's
own configuration, as nomic-ai/CodeRankEmbed publishes it under MIT. It
builds on the work below.

1. CodeRankEmbed (MIT), by Tarun Suresh, Revanth Gangi Reddy, Yifei Xu,
   Zach Nussbaum, Andriy Mulyar, Brandon Duderstadt and Heng Ji: the
   encoder trained on CoRNStack, whose NomicBERT architecture and
   sentence-transformers pooling this crate reproduces.
   https://huggingface.co/nomic-ai/CodeRankEmbed
   https://github.com/gangiswag/cornstack

2. XNNPACK (BSD-3-Clause), by Facebook, Inc. and its affiliates and Google
   LLC. The exponential under the softmax and the sigmoid computes as
   XNNPACK's f32 "p5" kernels do for finite values: the same constants and
   argument reduction, written anew in Rust (src/math.rs). The left operand
   of every matrix product is read through row pointers, as XNNPACK's
   indirect convolution reads it (src/gemm.rs).
   https://github.com/google/XNNPACK
   XNNPACK's license follows as notice A.


A. XNNPACK, https://github.com/google/XNNPACK

